  "notes": "Source: PROP-W5B14-17, Trust Boundary: tb-003, Source Threat: stride-004. The recovery function DOES NOT verify commitment consistency - this MUST be done by the caller. Missing verification turns validator into attack vector."
}
{
  "check_id": "W7B8:W7B8:CHK-0142",
  "title": "Supporting Check: Do ALL callers of recover_cells_and_kzg_proofs verify recovered data against original commitment?",
  "test_procedure": "1. Find all call sites of recover_cells_and_kzg_proofs in the codebase. 2. For EACH caller, verify it calls verify_cell_kzg_proof after recovery completes. 3. Check that verification uses the ORIGINAL commitment (passed from external source, not recomputed from recovered data). 4. Verify the caller handles verification failure by: (a) discarding recovered data, (b) NOT propagating to other peers, (c) potentially penalizing the source peer. 5. Look for any caller that uses recovered data before verification (race condition). 6. Check wrapper functions that may hide the recovery call - verify they also enforce verification. 7. Audit any async/concurrent recovery paths for missing verification.",
  "notes": "Source: PROP-W5B14-17, Trust Boundary: tb-003. The post-condition explicitly states the recovery function does NOT verify - caller MUST do it."
