  "title": "Supporting Check: Can a malicious P2P peer cause a validator to distribute corrupted recovered cells?",
  "test_procedure": "1. Set up test network with honest validator and malicious peer. 2. Malicious peer provides corrupted cells with valid cell_indices for a known blob. 3. Trigger recovery on the honest validator using the corrupted cells. 4. Observe if the validator: (a) detects corruption via commitment verification, (b) rejects the recovered data, (c) does NOT propagate corrupted cells to network. 5. If verification is missing, observe if corrupted cells are gossipped to other peers. 6. Measure propagation: how many nodes accept the corrupted data before detection? 7. Verify peer scoring: is the malicious peer penalized for providing data that fails verification? 8. Test with different corruption patterns: single bit flip, random garbage, partially valid data.",
  "notes": "Source: PROP-W5B14-17, Trust Boundary: tb-003, Covered Node: actor-p2p-peer. Bug bounty eligible: PoC showing node distributing corrupted cells after recovery from attacker-provided data."
}
