  "check_id": "W7B8:W7B8:CHK-0144",
  "title": "Supporting Check: Does the validator node trust reconstructed data without cryptographic verification?",
  "test_procedure": "1. Trace the data flow after recover_cells_and_kzg_proofs returns. 2. Identify all places where recovered cells are used: local storage, consensus, gossip. 3. For each usage, verify that KZG commitment verification PRECEDES the usage. 4. Check if any internal caching stores recovered cells before verification. 5. Verify that recovered proofs are also verified (not just cells). 6. Check for implicit trust: does the validator assume recovery success implies data validity? 7. Audit the relationship between SG-023 (recover_polynomialcoeff) and SG-024 (recover_cells_and_kzg_proofs) - ensure the proof generation is verified. 8. Verify the validator does not use recovered data for any consensus-critical operation before verification.",
  "notes": "Source: PROP-W5B14-17, Trust Boundary: tb-003, Covered Node: actor-validator-node. Severity justification: missing verification turns validator into distribution vector for invalid data."
}
{
  "check_id": "W7B8:W7B8:CHK-0145",
  "title": "Supporting Check: Is the 'original_commitment' used for verification sourced from trusted consensus, not recovered data?",
  "test_procedure": "1. Identify where 'original_commitment' comes from when verify_cell_kzg_proof is called. 2. Trace the commitment source: it MUST come from finalized beacon block header, NOT from the recovery process. 3. Verify the commitment is fetched from local trusted state (beacon chain head). 4. Check that the commitment cannot be influenced by the attacker's P2P messages. 5. Verify no code path allows using a commitment provided by the same peer that provided corrupted cells. 6. Test: provide corrupted cells AND a fake commitment that would make verification pass - verify this is rejected. 7. Ensure the commitment lookup is atomic with the verification to prevent TOCTOU. 8. Verify the commitment is pinned to a specific block/slot that the cells should belong to.",
  "notes": "Source: PROP-W5B14-17, Trust Boundary: tb-003. If attacker controls both cells AND commitment reference, verification is meaningless."
}

