BATCH_ITEMS:
1. CHK-0131 (PROP-W5B14-14): Cell Withholding Attack - Can a P2P peer withhold cells to trigger incorrect polynomial recovery?
2. CHK-0132 (PROP-W5B14-14): Blast Radius - What is the blast radius if recovery proceeds with insufficient cells?
3. CHK-0133 (PROP-W5B14-14): Ordering - Is the cell count pre-condition checked before all other operations?
4. CHK-0134 (PROP-W5B14-15): Cell Indices Uniqueness - Are cell_indices validated for uniqueness and ascending order before polynomial recovery?
5. CHK-0135 (PROP-W5B14-15): Polynomial Interpolation - Does polynomial interpolation assume unique, sorted cell_indices?
6. CHK-0136 (PROP-W5B14-15): Duplicate Injection - Can an attacker inject duplicate cell_indices via P2P gossip?
7. CHK-0137 (PROP-W5B14-16): Cell Index Range - Are all cell_indices validated to be in [0, CELLS_PER_EXT_BLOB) before polynomial recovery begins?
8. CHK-0138 (PROP-W5B14-16): Out-of-Range Crash - Does coset_for_cell crash or produce undefined behavior with out-of-range cell_index?
9. CHK-0139 (PROP-W5B14-16): Out-of-Range Injection via P2P - Can an attacker inject out-of-range cell_indices via P2P gossip to crash a node?
10. CHK-0140 (PROP-W5B14-16): Validation Order - Is cell_index range validation performed before resource allocation in recovery?
11. CHK-0141 (PROP-W5B14-17): Post-Recovery KZG Verification - Is post-recovery KZG commitment verification performed for ALL recovered cells and proofs?
12. CHK-0142 (PROP-W5B14-17): Caller Verification - Do ALL callers of recover_cells_and_kzg_proofs verify recovered data against original commitment?
13. CHK-0143 (PROP-W5B14-17): Corrupted Cell Distribution - Can a malicious P2P peer cause a validator to distribute corrupted recovered cells?
14. CHK-0144 (PROP-W5B14-17): Implicit Trust - Does the validator node trust reconstructed data without cryptographic verification?
15. CHK-0145 (PROP-W5B14-17): Commitment Source - Is the 'original_commitment' used for verification sourced from trusted consensus, not recovered data?

